# NitrOS-9 for Fujitsu FM-11

[日本語版](README.md)

This repository contains a port of [NitrOS-9](https://github.com/nitros9project/nitros9) for the Fujitsu FM-11.

It is maintained as a fork of the upstream NitrOS-9 source tree. FM-11-specific implementations are kept separate where practical so that upstream changes can continue to be incorporated.

## Current status

The basic ports of **NitrOS-9 Level 1 and Level 2** for the FM-11 are complete.

Both the Motorola 6809 and Hitachi HD63C09 builds have been tested booting from 2D and 2HD floppy images and running normal system operations.

### Level 1

The Level 1 port currently includes:

- Motorola 6809 support
- Hitachi HD63C09 support, including native mode
- FM-11 local console
- USART0 serial terminal `/T1`
- 5.25-inch 2D floppy support
- 5.25-inch 2HD floppy support
- FM-11 hard disk interface support
- RBF / RBSuper
- Pipes
- ANSI / VT100 terminal support
- `format`
- `cobbler`
- `os9gen`
- `more`
- MinTED / dEd
- Standard commands, disk utilities, and diagnostic tools

FM-11-specific Level 1 sources are primarily located under:

```text
level1/fm11/
```

### Level 2

The Level 2 port combines pairs of the FM-11's 4 KiB MMR pages and exposes them to NitrOS-9 as normal 8 KiB DAT blocks.

The current implementation includes:

- Motorola 6809 support
- Hitachi HD63C09 support
- 8 KiB-pair MMU implementation using 4 KiB FM-11 MMR pages
- FM-11 kernel trampoline
- FM-11 local console
- USART0 serial terminal `/T1`
- 5.25-inch 2D floppy support
- 5.25-inch 2HD floppy support
- RBF / RBSuper
- Pipes and Shell pipelines
- ANSI / VT100 terminal support
- `format`
- `cobbler`
- `os9gen`
- Level 2 memory and process diagnostic commands
- 6809 and 6309 system-image generation

FM-11-specific Level 2 sources are primarily located under:

```text
level2/fm11/
```

The current Level 2 default boot lists do not include the hard-disk modules. The Level 2 system images currently distributed by this port therefore target floppy booting. HDD-related low-level code and descriptors remain in the source tree.

## Build requirements

The FM-11 build primarily requires:

- [LWTOOLS](http://lwtools.projects.l-w.ca/), including `lwasm`
- [ToolShed](https://github.com/n6il/toolshed), including the `os9` command
- Python 3
- Standard Unix command-line utilities

The build scripts are intended for a Linux/Unix-like environment.

## Building

Clone the repository:

```sh
git clone https://github.com/sueyasu/fm11-nitros9.git
cd fm11-nitros9
```

The common FM-11 image-build entry point is:

```sh
scripts/fm11/build-images.sh LEVEL CPU [MEDIA]
```

Accepted values are:

```text
LEVEL : 1 | 2
CPU   : 6809 | 6309
MEDIA : 2d | 2hd | all
```

If `MEDIA` is omitted, `all` is used.

### Level 1

Build the 6809 2D and 2HD images with:

```sh
scripts/fm11/build-images.sh 1 6809
```

For the 6309:

```sh
scripts/fm11/build-images.sh 1 6309
```

Generated files:

```text
fm11-l1-6809-2d.rbf
fm11-l1-6809-2d.d88
fm11-l1-6809-2hd.rbf
fm11-l1-6809-2hd.d88

fm11-l1-6309-2d.rbf
fm11-l1-6309-2d.d88
fm11-l1-6309-2hd.rbf
fm11-l1-6309-2hd.d88
```

### Level 2

For the 6809:

```sh
scripts/fm11/build-images.sh 2 6809
```

For the 6309:

```sh
scripts/fm11/build-images.sh 2 6309
```

Generated files:

```text
fm11-l2-6809-2d.rbf
fm11-l2-6809-2d.d88
fm11-l2-6809-2hd.rbf
fm11-l2-6809-2hd.d88

fm11-l2-6309-2d.rbf
fm11-l2-6309-2d.d88
fm11-l2-6309-2hd.rbf
fm11-l2-6309-2hd.d88
```

To build only one media profile, for example:

```sh
scripts/fm11/build-images.sh 2 6809 2d
```

## Floppy configuration

The physical device names are common to Level 1 and Level 2:

```text
/MD0, /MD1 = 5.25-inch 2D
/ND0, /ND1 = 5.25-inch 2HD
```

Level 1 also uses logical `/D0` through `/D3` aliases according to the selected system profile.

2D system:

```text
/D0, /D1 = 2D
/D2, /D3 = 2HD
```

2HD system:

```text
/D0, /D1 = 2HD
/D2, /D3 = 2D
```

The current Level 2 boot lists do not keep the `/D0` through `/D3` alias descriptors resident, in order to keep OS9Boot small. Use `/MD0`, `/MD1`, `/ND0`, and `/ND1` directly.

## `/SYS` layout

The FM-11 port uses the same `/SYS` layout convention for Level 1 and Level 2.

Typical layout:

```text
/SYS/IPL/
    IPL.2D
    IPL.2HD
    IPL.HD

/SYS/BOOT/
    Bootp1.2D
    Bootp1.2HD
    Bootp1.HD

/SYS/MODULES/
    ... modules used to generate boot files ...

/SYS/bootlist.2d
/SYS/bootlist.2hd
```

`cobbler` and `os9gen` read these files through `/DD/SYS`.

The pathname convention is common between Level 1 and Level 2, but the file contents are not necessarily interchangeable. In particular, the Level 2 Bootp1 files contain the Level 2 kernel track with REL, Boot, and Krn.

## FM-11 boot layout

The FM-11 port uses floppy cylinder 0 as a reserved boot area outside the normal RBF filesystem area.

For Level 2, the IPL loads a kernel track containing REL, Boot, and Krn, after which OS9Boot is loaded and the system starts.

The FM-11 versions of `format`, `cobbler`, and `os9gen` understand this IPL and boot-track layout.

## Source layout

Important FM-11-specific files are located under:

```text
defs/fm11.d
level1/fm11/
level2/fm11/
scripts/fm11/
```

### Level 1

```text
level1/fm11/
    bootlists/   boot module lists
    cmds/        FM-11-specific commands, ports, and diagnostics
    ipl/         FM-11 IPL code
    modules/     drivers, descriptors, boot and console modules
    sys/         FM-11-specific system files
```

### Level 2

```text
level2/fm11/
    bootlists/   Level 2 boot module lists
    ipl/         FM-11 Level 2 IPL code
    kernel/      FM-11-specific kernel support
    modules/     MMU, boot, drivers, descriptors, and related modules
```

Shared upstream sources are used directly where appropriate. Substantially modified FM-11-specific sources are kept under `level1/fm11/` or `level2/fm11/` whenever practical.

## Level 2 MMU model

NitrOS-9 Level 2 normally manages memory in 8 KiB DAT blocks, while the FM-11 MMR works in 4 KiB pages.

The FM-11 Level 2 port maps each OS-9 8 KiB block to a pair of consecutive 4 KiB MMR pages:

```text
OS-9 block 0 -> FM-11 MMR slots 0,1
OS-9 block 1 -> FM-11 MMR slots 2,3
OS-9 block 2 -> FM-11 MMR slots 4,5
...
OS-9 block 7 -> FM-11 MMR slots E,F
```

This preserves the normal NitrOS-9 Level 2 8 KiB memory-management model as far as practical while adapting it to the FM-11 hardware.

## Known notes

- The current Level 2 default configuration targets floppy booting.
- A size-sensitive issue has been observed in the Level 2 initial OS9Boot load path, so the default boot lists intentionally keep the resident module set compact.
- When adding modules to a Level 2 boot list, keep the total OS9Boot size in mind.
- Some FM-11 emulator versions differ in their HD63C09 instruction implementation. Use an emulator version with the required 6309 fixes when testing the 6309 build.

## Versioning

GitHub-based versioning of this FM-11 port begins with:

```text
fm11-v0.1
```

Earlier internal version and test numbers used during initial bring-up are development history and are not part of the Git tag versioning scheme.

## Upstream

This repository is based on the NitrOS-9 project:

[NitrOS-9 Project](https://github.com/nitros9project/nitros9)

Upstream changes can continue to be incorporated while the FM-11-specific port is maintained in this repository.

